@startuml fig1_process_structure
' Diagram 1 of the VDI 3682 pattern: the process and how it decomposes.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md. Flat boxes, no namespace prefixes, no clause
' numbers, orthogonal edges, nothing explanatory inside the drawing.
'
' What it shows: what a process consists of, how an operator is refined into
' further operators, and how the operators are ordered in time.
'
' Two relations that look alike are kept apart here. consistsOf reaches from a
' process to what it holds, isComposedOf refines one operator into others, and
' hasUpperProcess and hasSubProcess tie the levels of Figure 5 together. A
' model uses all three at once, which is why they appear side by side.
'
' The order relations are drawn as self-edges on the operator, since a
' predecessor and a successor are operators like any other. Part 1, Figure 4
' connects operators through states rather than directly, so the order is
' stated alongside the flow rather than derived from it.
'
' Of each inverse pair only one is drawn. hasUpperProcess and hasPredecessor
' say what hasSubProcess and hasSuccessor already say, read from the other end,
' and drawing both would put two labels in one place for one statement. The
' ontology declares all four.
'
' Left out on purpose:
'  - the states themselves and what carries them: diagram 2
'  - resources and their assignment: diagram 3

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 45
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 14
  BorderThickness 1
}

class Process
class ProcessOperator
class SystemLimit

' A process holds operators. Only one direction of the level relation is drawn:
' hasSubProcess and hasUpperProcess are two readings of the same tie between
' the coarse and the refined view of Figure 5, and drawing both puts two labels
' in one place for one statement.
Process         -down->  "*" ProcessOperator : consistsOf
ProcessOperator -right-> "*" Process         : hasSubProcess

' Refinement and order both run from an operator to an operator, so both are
' self-edges. hasPredecessor is left out for the same reason as above: it is
' hasSuccessor read backwards.
ProcessOperator -left->  "*" ProcessOperator : isComposedOf
ProcessOperator -up->    "*" ProcessOperator : hasSuccessor

ProcessOperator --> "*" SystemLimit : isWithin

@enduml
